{
    "file_name": "AFP_ENG_20051209.0109.tml",
    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_20051209.0109\n\nLEIPZIG, Germany, Dec 9 , 2005\n\nIran coach backs Portuguese for semi-finals\n\n\n\n\nIran coach Branko Ivankovic believes Group D rivals and Euro 2004 runners-up Portugal can make the World Cup semi-finals.\n\n\"Our group contains very good teams,\" said the Croatian.\n\n\"The favourite is clearly Portugal, they will be in the semi-finals.\n\n\"Mexico are a good side, I was very impressed by them at the Confederations Cup. Angola are a new team to me. They have a lot of enthusiasm and a game which is difficult to understand.\n\n\"I am proud of my team, we have worked hard recently. Our problem will be in adapting to the different styles - European, African and Latin-American. I hope our players will learn how to respond to the different problems.\"",
